lth-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity and walks the entire v2/v3/v4 R&D surface fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching port 8777), writing dated reports and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Design constraint.** Python stdlib only (sole exception: the optional `pywinpty` terminal extra), all data human-readable markdown/JSON, accessible from any CLI or editor â€” enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87d85095-5cd6-4ea6-a34e-9b2c847810e5","uuid":"76918d40-9c32-4ec9-bffa-f5908f79a72c","request_id":"req_011Cc1YsUo3hU3LjGn11Rtyw"}
